WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.832 --> 00:00:06.665
(lively instrumental music)

00:00:06.665 --> 00:00:09.010
- [Narrator] This is the
beginning of a kimono.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.990
One of the world's most precious kimonos,

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.780
a thousand-year-old fashion statement

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:18.040
that all starts here in the mud
on a unique tropical island.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.063
This is the kimono world's
dirty little secret.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.140
This story starts in Ginza,

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.100
a neighborhood in Tokyo known for fashion,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.323
and home to a famous kimono shop.

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:07.490
- [Narrator] In the 1700s,
Japan invaded Amami Ōshima,

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:09.250
and everyone was forced to surrender

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.280
all of their silk kimonos
to Japan's ruling class.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.400
So, legend has it that
the people of Amami Ōshima

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.140
hid their kimonos in the mud

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.093
and discovered that they were
dyed a beautiful black color.

00:02:08.651 --> 00:02:10.620
- [Narrator] Some say the
heritage behind these kimonos

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.423
is just as sacred as the kimono itself.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:42.108
(lively instrumental music)

